Problem Link : https://leetcode.com/problems/smallest-divisible-digit-product-i/description/

class Solution:
    def smallestNumber(self, n: int, t: int) -> int:

        def digit_product(num):
            product = 1
            while num:
                product *= num % 10
                num //= 10
            return product

        for i in range(n, n + 11):
            if digit_product(i) % t == 0:
                return i

        return -1

''' time complexity : O(k * logn)  [k = at most 10 numbers, logn = digits per number]
    space complexity : O(1)

    - helper function extracts digit product via mod 10 and floor divide
    - iterate from n to n+10 (guaranteed answer within 10 steps)
    - reason: next number with a 0 digit has product 0, divisible by anything
    - return first number whose digit_product is divisible by t
